r job of setting up at central  quest story it failed to sell the deeper  conflicts inherent in the epic journey  of the characters and felt incomplete  speaking of which run time run nowadays  viewers who walk into big budget  blockbusters expect to be in the  theaters for at least two hours and  often more The Dark Tower easily could  have filled up this runtime in fact it  probably would have helped it's awkward  attempt to fit so many disparate  elements from kings novels into one  movie  I'm uestion alone in the library a lot  director Nick our cell however decided  to instead keep the film in a very tight  ninety five minutes the director said he  did this because he saw the film as an  introduction to the world of the novel's  adding that the movie had a lean script  that would introduce the basic ideas of  the project without being too  overwhelming at first  while this runtime may have been doable  had our cell chosen to only focus on the  first book the movies decision to mix  and match elements from all of Kings  books is a pseudo sequel meant it had to  introduce huge amounts of information  while playing out its story although  ourself saw the short run time as a way  to build the world without doing too  much  some sod is being too brief leaving the  world feeling empty and unfinished the  movie could have benefited from an extra  30 minutes of world-building if not more  filmmaking fracas our cell wasn't the  first director to try his hand in  adapting the dark hour in 2007 JJ Abrams  pulled together his lost pals Carlton  Cuse and Damon Lindelof who were also  big fans of Stephen King but they ended  up letting go the adaptation option  because they were too nervous about  messing up the love at work  that's when Ron Howard stepped up to the  plate with a plan for three movies and a  TV series to bring the story to life the  project was set up at Universal Pictures  but the studio pulled the plug on that  expensive idea and it took three more  years 